{title: That They May Be One}
{subtitle: John 17:20–21}
{key: Bb}
{tempo: 70}
{time: 4/4}

{comment: Intro}
| [Bb] | [F/A] | [Gm7] | [Eb] |
| [F] |

{start_of_verse: Verse 1}
[Bb]I pray not for these a[Eb]lone to[F]day
[Gm]But for those [Eb]who will be[Bb]lieve
Through the word [Bb/D]that they con[Eb]vey
In[Gm]to the [F]world to re[Eb]ceive
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 2}
[Bb]As you the Fa[Bb/D]ther are in [Eb]me
[Gm]And I am in [Eb]you like[Bb]wise
Let them [Bb/D]be in us, we [Eb]sing
In this [Gm]holy, [F]quiet [Eb]space
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_chorus: Chorus}
That they may all be [Bb]one
As we are [F]one, as we are [Gm]one
Let the world believe [Eb]it is done
That you sent [Bb]me, [F]and this is [Bb]won
{end_of_chorus}

{start_of_verse: Verse 3}
The glory [Bb/D]you gave to [Eb]me
[Gm]I have [Eb]given to them [Bb]all
That they may [Bb/D]be complete and [Eb]free
In [Gm]truth and [F]in the [Eb]call
{end_of_verse}

{chorus}

{start_of_bridge: Bridge}
[Eb]I in them and you in [Gm]me
[Eb]Brought to complete uni[Bb]ty [Bb/D]
[Eb]So the world may know with [Gm]ease
That you loved [F]them as I
{end_of_bridge}

{start_of_verse: Outro}
That they may all be [Bb]one
[F]As you and I are [Bb]one [Eb]
{end_of_verse}
